  <title xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">First Public Investment Reform Sppt Cr.</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="2" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">- Improve the quality, reliability and accountability of the country&apos;s PFM and PIM systems; - Establish the policy and regulatory framework necessary for a well-functioning public irrigation sector, including a model for the multipurpose operation of the Kandadji Dam; - Facilitate the reform of the electricity sector.</narrative>
  </description>
  <description type="1" xml:lang="EN">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objectives of the First Public Investment Reform Support Credit (PIRSC) to the Government of Niger are: (i) to improve the quality, reliability and accountability of the country&apos;s Public Finance Management (PFM) and Public Investment Management (PIM) system; (ii) to establish the policy and regulatory framework necessary for a well-functioning public irrigation sector, including a model for the multipurpose operation of the Kandadji Dam; and (iii) to facilitate the reform of the electricity sector. Building on the reform agenda supported by the previous shared growth development policy operation, the PIRSC series is structured around three pillars: (1) strengthening PFM and PIM systems; (2) improving the management of the public irrigation sector; and (3) enhancing the institutional framework for the electricity sector. The series which will consist of three single tranche credits to be disbursed over the year 2016 to 2018.</narrative>
  </description>
